From 98314491192f9ce7eb96e71b07fe5d8e59be5dc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <winshyon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:05:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(eval): use the newest eval row per benchmark for registry
 baselines

resolve_baseline kept the last row it saw for each benchmark, and
get_eval_results returns rows newest first, so a registry baseline used the
oldest score while its provenance warning came from the newest stamped row.
Re-measuring the baseline, as the warning asks, silenced the warning and
kept the stale score, letting a real regression pass the gate.

Take both the score and the provenance from each benchmark's newest row,
check provenance per benchmark (naming the stale ones), and make the
created_at tie-break explicit with rowid DESC.

Closes #1224
